# Brief: diff 5e3c12b~3

## TL;DR
- The diff adds two new skills (`skills/debug-loop/SKILL.md`, `skills/p-review/SKILL.md`), a rewritten adversarial-review skill (`skills/adversarial-review-2/`), a plan for a `brief-artifact` skill, and three research docs under `resources/`; it edits one existing file (`skills/adversarial-review/SKILL.md`) to point at adversarial-review-2.
- Roughly 50 of 61 chunks are generated eval workspace output (benchmark.json/md, grading.json, timing.json, metrics.json, run transcripts) for adversarial-review-2 and debug-loop; the headline numbers all favor with_skill (100% vs 67-92%), each from a single run per configuration, so the reported stddevs rest on two data points.
- The only executable code is `skills/debug-loop-workspace/grade.py` plus the debug-loop eval fixtures; grade.py hardcodes an absolute `/Users/admin/...` fixture path and its `test_first` and `source_otherwise_unchanged` checks are brittle to unrelated file or whitespace changes.
- Every eval run commits byte-identical `timing.json` (and often grading/metrics) at both `run-1/` and the parent directory, and several `outputs/project` entries are gitlinks to dirty submodule commits, so that content is not reproducible from this diff.
- No claim contradicts another across chunks; benchmark.md summaries match their benchmark.json sources in each iteration.

