This chunk adds three new files for an eval iteration of the adversarial-review-2 skill. benchmark.md reports pass rate, time, and token deltas between with-skill and without-skill runs, with a caveat that results come from a single run per eval. eval_metadata.json defines a red-team eval prompt asking the skill to review a checkout session-cache design with severities and a retest mechanism, listing nine required findings/behaviors. session-cache-design.md is the target design doc itself: a Redis session-pricing cache with TTL, KEYS-based invalidation, and sizing that consumes all free memory on a shared cluster.

