This chunk adds two new eval fixture files and an evals.json for a new 'adversarial-review-2' skill, then edits the existing adversarial-review SKILL.md description. evals.json defines two evals: a red-team of a Redis session-cache design (checkout pricing) and of a follow-the-sun on-call rotation plan, each with a prompt and a list of expected-output checks covering severity grading, ranked findings, retest mechanisms, and specific planted flaws (KEYS-based cache invalidation, sizing math, timezone coverage gap, US-only IC pool). The two new markdown fixture files contain the actual design/plan documents being evaluated. The SKILL.md diff trims wording and adds a new 'Do NOT use' clause pointing severity-graded/retest-loop requests to adversarial-review-2.

### chunk-31 [high] skills/debug-loop-workspace/grade.py:1+ (diff)

New file skills/debug-loop-workspace/grade.py: a mechanical eval grader for debug-loop runs. It walks eval-*/{with_skill,without_skill,old_skill}/outputs directories, reads each run's response.md and git history in the project fixture, runs the pytest suite, and computes signals like whether a debug brief heading/fields were present, whether tests were committed before the fix, and suite pass/fail. It then branches per eval name (vague-login, traceback, trivial-typo, red-tests) to check task-specific behaviors (e.g. version- vs created_at-based selection, BOM-aware reads, typo fix without other changes, unchanged pricing assertions with Decimal/cents usage). Emits one JSON blob per run.

