### chunk-02 [low] resources/good-adversarial-review.md:1+ (diff)

This diff adds a new file, resources/good-adversarial-review.md, a research document defining what makes a good adversarial review (red team/safety evaluation) of AI chatbots. It argues quality comes from discipline, not clever jailbreaks: explicit impact-anchored scope, diverse and partly independent teams, taxonomy-anchored reproducible methodology, manual plus automated testing, severity grading, and a closed remediation-retest loop run continuously. It synthesizes NIST, OWASP, MITRE ATLAS, and lab practices (Microsoft, OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepMind), lists common pitfalls of weak reviews, gives a four-stage recommendation, and closes with caveats about field immaturity, metric fragility, and reliance on vendor sources.

